From 4e73f0c9abf638aada2804c60355e85cd0d14d56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:22:29 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] kcm_kwin_effects: page shown before the effect scan,
 empty/busy states, no opacity text; labels unchanged
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: List (ScrollViewKCM: search, category sections, per-effect Configure… as inline action, Get New… top right);
already the right type, so structure and wording stay. kwinrc keys, effect config dialogs, KNS and excluded effects
unchanged. Overview, Invert and colour blindness correction stay here (ia/duplicates.md): nothing removed. NOT BUILT YET.

Changes:
- DesktopEffectsKCM::load() no longer scans on the first call: ui/main.qml calls the new kcm.startLoading() on the first
  frameSwapped of its window (a 1.5 s timer calls it if no QML does); later load() calls (Reset, GHNS) scan as before.
  New property `loading` (true until EffectsModel::loaded).
- While the list is empty: QQC2.BusyIndicator after 150 ms of loading; Kirigami.PlaceholderMessage "No effects match
  your search" / "No effects found" afterwards (HIG empty states).
- Effect rows: description/author lines use Kirigami.Theme.smallFont instead of opacity 0.6/0.8 (page-design.md 3);
  checkbox/radio got Accessible.name = effect name, Configure button Accessible.name "Configure <effect>…";
  search field Accessible.name.
HIG ids: HIG-001, HIG-023, empty-state and accessibility rows; page-design.md 3, 4, 7.

Speed cause (code evidence): inventory/structure notes and common/effectsmodel.cpp:373-380: load() runs
loadBuiltInEffects (QDirIterator over JSON, :214), loadJavascriptEffects (KPackage scan, :272) and loadPluginEffects
(KPluginMetaData::findPlugins, :317) synchronously, then publishes the model only after the async areEffectsSupported
reply (:430). All of it ran in DesktopEffectsKCM::load() before the page could draw; now the empty page draws first.
Note the scan itself still blocks the GUI thread once, right after the first frame (making it incremental needs changes
in the shared EffectsModel, not done). After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet.
Unconfirmed: Window.window / frameSwapped from a ScrollViewKCM root (attached Window property on an Item); that load()
is called after construction and before the UI exists in systemsettings (assumed from KQuickConfigModule).
inventory_check --strict still lists unchanged weak-anchor rows in plugin .ui files (not touched); without --strict 0 lost,
and the two rows of this page's QML (search, Configure-Filter) carry markers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
